				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1191,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Common): Introduce health monitoring data models and score logic\n\nDefine the core data structures for the editor's health monitoring subsystem within `Source/IPC/Common/HealthStatus`. This commit adds `SeverityLevel::Enum` to classify issue criticality, `HealthIssue::Enum` as a tagged union for specific failure modes (e.g., MemoryPressure, ConnectionLoss), and `HealthMonitor::Struct` to aggregate state.\n\nThe `HealthMonitor` calculates a dynamic `HealthScore` (0-100) based on a deterministic penalty system derived from issue severities (Low: -5, Medium: -15, High: -25, Critical: -40). It provides methods for adding/removing issues, filtering by severity, and determining overall system health status (`IsHealthy`, `IsCritical`). All types derive `Serialize`/`Deserialize` to enable transmission over the gRPC (Vine) and Tauri IPC channels for real-time status propagation to the Wind and Sky layers.\n\nThese models lay the foundation for the backend to expose service liveness metrics to the frontend without blocking the main thread.",
			"SHA": "23d6eddefce6d663ef87fdd01e468309c773f80d"
		}
